    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nSuppose we have the following strings:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"hello \\\"world\\\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nputting cursor inside this string and let's see the behavior of `mini.ai`\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nminimal config:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup {search_method = \"cover\"}\r\nvim.highlight.on_yank { higroup = 'IncSearch', timeout = 400 }\r\n-- we use `cover` method to understand what's under the hood mini.ai is doing under current context\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nIf `mini.ai` is not installed, this is the default behavior in vim:\r\n\r\nNo matter where the cursor position is in, as long as cursor is inside `hello \\\"world\\\"`, then `ya\"` will select `\"hello \\\"world\\\"\"`,\r\n\r\nand `yi\"` will select `hello \\\"world\\\"`\r\n\r\nThis option is more acceptable than current `mini.ai`'s implementation.\r\n\r\nA more ideal way would be:\r\n\r\nwhen cursor is at `hel|lo`, where `|` is the cursor position, typing `yaq or ya\"` should select `\"hello \\\"world\\\"\"`, and when cursor is at `wor|ld`, `yaq or ya\"` should select `\"world\"` or `\\\"world\\\"` (I think either two cases are resonable).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nHowever, in `mini.ai`, this is the behavior:\r\n\r\ncursor position 1:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"he|llo \\\"world\\\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\npress `yi\"` select `hello \\`,\r\n\r\ncursor position 2:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"hello \\\"wo|rld\\\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\npress `yi\"` will yield an error: `No textobject \"ia\" found covering region within 100 lines and `search_method = 'cover'`.`",
