            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe behavior you describe does sound nicer than current verbatim quote treatment of quotes. But I doubt there is a concise yet effective way to account for it under current Lua pattern based matching. It certainly is possible, but might require callable textobject specification, which is not ideal.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it, but I don't have high hopes about this being implemented.\r\n\r\nSide note: same remark goes for `'` and possibly for `` ` ``; maybe even for all kinds of parenthesis.",
