        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I understand. Lua pattern match is less powerful than regex.\r\n> \r\n> Can we have a blacklist (fallback) config option? That is, if I specified `\"` as part of this config, then when I press `a\"` or `i'` then it will use the default vim way rather than using mini?\r\n\r\nIt is already possible by [setting `custom_textobject` entry to `false`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/56509def588044fd5dcd1efe74197f1f4fe8953a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L441-L442).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Besides, When putting at cursor position2 (inside the escaped quote), `a\"` and `i\"` in mini don’t select anything but yield an error. May I consider this as a bug?\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce any error.\r\n\r\nIf you have `No textobject \"ia\" found ...`, as in original post, then you typed `ia` instead of `i\"`.\r\n\r\nIf you execute `yi\"`, it shows message `Textobject region is empty. Nothing is done.`. This is because when cursor is on `world`, it tries to copy **inside** the following `\"\"` (which is the the next match here, as quotes are balanced). This is expected.",
            "created_at": "2023-06-13T13:13:20Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/366#issuecomment-1589289533",
